prepareLakesideJourney: after mountLakesideScenery -> applyLakesideJourneyBatching(model,{enableLakesideInstancing, mergeLakesideStatic,
lakesideStaticMergeFromEnv, isLakesideWaterNode}); water GLBs (tagged at mount) stay out of the merge; ?lakemerge=off keeps instancing
only. Merged meshes + instanced material copies are freed exactly once in the lease's release() (leave/returnToIsland, controller
dispose, abandonLakesideJourney friendly fallback, prepare failure). Expected journey lakeside draws ~431+ -> ~4 (same plan as the board:
2 palette chunks + 1 unmerged + water); extra ~1.6 MB merged mesh while board + journey copies coexist (accepted by lead). Far scenery
not hidden. Test lakeside-journey-merge.
